    ("language-race-consequences", "Race consequences belong to a named language", "C++20 and Rust 1.90 impose undefined behavior for their scoped data races. Java retains its execution and causality rules, while Go permits reporting and terminating a race and otherwise constrains scalar observations. A Go composite race can nevertheless produce an inconsistent descriptor and arbitrary memory corruption.", "undefined-execution"),
