    ("go-channel-direction-boundary", "Channel ordering depends on the matched event and capacity", "Every Go send orders completion of its matching receive, including a sent zero. Close orders a receive that observes closed-and-drained state. The reverse receive-to-send-completion edge applies directly to an unbuffered channel; a capacity-C channel instead supplies the kth-receive to (k+C)th-send rule. Goroutine exit by itself supplies no join edge.", "go-receive"),
    ("rust-documented-model-boundary", "Rust atomic documentation is not a complete unsafe-code proof", "Rust 1.90 follows a documented access-based translation of C++20 atomics without consume and has target-dependent atomic availability. Its full unsafe and aliasing model remains unfinished. Every positive atomic example here also assumes valid provenance, lifetime, alignment, aliasing, and type-sharing obligations; ordering alone does not establish them.", "rust-atomic"),
    ("resource-model-boundary", "A resource cycle needs instance and release assumptions", "The sufficient deadlock example is a closed set of blocked holders of distinct single-instance locks, with no external release, cancellation, or preemption. A cycle between resource types with multiple available instances can be resolvable. Strict acquisition ranks remove that lock-cycle mechanism without proving fairness or excluding waits on other resources.", "wait-cycle"),
